cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus or benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "forecast-answer-formats: a cross-tool benchmark of forecasting-bot answer extractors"
abstract: >-
  A public labeled corpus comparing which valid LLM answer formats deployed
  forecasting-bot extractors (mv2-forecaster, Metaculus forecasting-tools, and
  a third tournament entrant, EskemoMan/metaculus-forecast-bot) read versus
  silently drop, and when they misread reasoning text as a spurious forecast,
  across all three Metaculus question types: binary, multiple-choice, and
  numeric (percentile); plus tested models of what a drop and a (binary or
  numeric) misread each cost in the tournament prize, unified under one law
  k = (log-score loss relative to a correct read) / mu.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "MV2 of Munim, Inc."
version: 0.11.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: CC-BY-4.0
